# retroforge built-in firmware list (CONFIG_EXTRA_FIRMWARE) — blobs baked into Image.gz so they
# are present before the rootfs mounts. One /lib/firmware-relative path per line; kernel/build.sh
# resolves each against firmware/linux-fw/ then firmware/qcom-fw/ and derives CONFIG_EXTRA_FIRMWARE
# from this list. Comments (#) and blank lines ignored.
#
# Empty: nothing needs firmware before the root mounts. msm-firmware-loader serves each device's
# own GPU firmware from its vendor partition (SQE/GMU/AQE as qcom/<name>, the zap shader as
# qcom/<soc>/<name>), and built-in firmware is searched first, so a copy here would shadow it. msm
# loads the GPU on first open and retries on the next one if that fails, so an open from the
# initramfs only defers it. DSPs, amp configs and topologies load after the root mounts too.
